<script lang="ts">
	import { englishExamples as examples } from '../../utils/examples.en'
</script>

<template>
	<DocsPage
		locale="en"
		title="Installation"
		description="Enable the module, set up the host and start with your first component."
	>
		<h2 id="requirements">Before you start</h2>
		<p>
			You need a Meeko application, Node.js 24 or later and a Meeko version in the range
			<code>&gt;=1.8 &lt;2</code>. UI belongs to the Meeko ecosystem and ships as a separate package.
		</p>
		<h2 id="install">Install the package</h2>
		<p>
			Install UI together with
			<code>tailwindcss</code>: your application compiles the styles of UI with its own Tailwind 4.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="Terminal"
			bind:code="examples.install"
		/>
		<h2 id="module">Register the module</h2>
		<p>
			Register it by name: its options go under the
			<code>ui</code>
			key, typed without importing anything. Components are registered with the
			<code>UI</code>
			prefix.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="meeko.config.ts"
			bind:code="examples.config"
		/>
		<h2 id="styles">Import the styles</h2>
		<p>
			Start
			<code>app/styles/main.css</code>, the global stylesheet that Meeko loads by itself, with Tailwind and the CSS entry of UI. They compile in one pass together with your classes: the theme of UI adds to Tailwind's, so you keep
			<code>bg-red-500</code>
			or
			<code>md:</code>
			and gain
			<code>bg-primary-9</code>,
			<code>text-danger-11</code>
			and the other steps of the semantic colors.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="app/styles/main.css"
			bind:code="examples.styles"
		/>
		<p>
			The module registers
			<code>@tailwindcss/vite</code>, unless your application already registers it, and serves the Inter font: you do not need another processor or to copy the font. Without these imports the components have no styles, and
			<code>meeko dev</code>
			warns you.
		</p>
		<p>
			For the 31 scales of Radix Colors (<code>bg-crimson-9</code>…) and the combinations of raw hues, add the optional entry
			<code>@meekojs/ui/hues</code>
			after them.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="app/styles/main.css"
			bind:code="examples.hues"
		/>
		<h3 id="preflight">With or without Tailwind's preflight</h3>
		<p>
			<code>@import 'tailwindcss'</code>
			brings the preflight, Tailwind's reset: it removes the margins of every element, the bullets of lists and the size and weight of headings. The UI components do not depend on it, but if your application did not use Tailwind it will change its look. To keep the previous one, import only Tailwind's theme and utilities, in the layers of its own entry.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="app/styles/main.css"
			bind:code="examples.stylesWithoutPreflight"
		/>
		<p>
			The UI base stays in place, and
			<code>ui.tokens</code>,
			<code>@meekojs/ui/hues</code>
			and the warning of
			<code>meeko dev</code>
			work the same with both forms.
		</p>
		<h2 id="host">Add UIApp</h2>
		<p>
			Wrap your application to host the modals opened with
			<code>useModal()</code>. The module's plugin creates the manager and
			<code>UIApp</code>
			renders its stack.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="app/app.meeko"
			bind:code="examples.app"
		/>
		<h2 id="first-component">Use a component</h2>
		<DocsPreview>
			<UIButton>Save changes</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				variant="outline"
				color="neutral">Cancel</UIButton>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.button" />
		<UIAlert tone="info">Signals, macros and UI components are discovered in your application. The types you need explicitly are imported from the package's public exports.</UIAlert>
		<p>
			Continue with
			<MeekoLink to="/theming">theming and customization</MeekoLink>
			or explore
			<MeekoLink to="/components">all components</MeekoLink>.
		</p>
	</DocsPage>
</template>
